# Rhizo Edge — Mosquitto access control (ADR-012 §Credentials).
#
# Order matters in this file: Mosquitto applies `user` blocks to that user and
# `pattern` rules to everyone. A device gets ONLY the pattern rules.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the edge
# The control plane reads every device's traffic and writes commands and
# retained config to every device's subtree. It is the only account with a
# fleet-wide view, and it is not a device.
user rhizo-edge
topic readwrite rhizo/v1/#

# --------------------------------------------------------------- every device
# The line that makes device identity a real boundary rather than a convention.
#
# `%u` is substituted with the *authenticated* username, and ADR-012 makes the
# username the `device_id`. A device authenticated as `plant-node-01` therefore
# cannot publish to, or subscribe to, `rhizo/v1/devices/plant-node-02/...` —
# the broker rejects it, with no cooperation required from the device.
#
# This is also why ADR-002 puts `device_id` before the message kind in the
# topic tree: `rhizo/v1/devices/{id}/telemetry` can be confined with one
# rule, while `rhizo/v1/telemetry/{id}` could not.
#
# Nothing else is granted. A device has no reason to see the fleet, and a
# compromised or simply buggy one must not be able to impersonate its
# neighbour or watch another plant's telemetry.
pattern readwrite rhizo/v1/devices/%u/#
